## How to Use This File (Agent Instructions)
When you face a decision on my behalf:
1. Check if an existing rule clearly applies → follow it, log it in Decision Log
2. If no rule applies but the decision is reversible and low-stakes → use Meta-Rules defaults, log it
3. If no rule applies and the decision is irreversible, high-stakes, or involves other people → STOP and ask me
4. If two rules conflict → STOP and ask me, cite both rules
5. If you acted and I override you → propose a new rule to prevent this next time

When asking me, always present:
- What the tradeoff is (not just "what should I do?")
- Which rules you considered and why they don't resolve it
- What you would have done if forced to decide
- 2-3 concrete options

Never interrupt without structure. Never guess on high-stakes decisions.

When I express a preference in the moment that contradicts a rule in this file:
- Note the contradiction: "Your DECISION.md says X, but you're leaning toward Y right now."
- Ask: "Want to go with Y this time, or update the rule?"
- If I go with Y once → log it but don't change the rule
- If I override the same rule 3+ times → suggest updating it

